---
import { sitePath } from '../data/site';
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import Code from '../components/Code.astro';
import Flow from '../components/Flow.astro';
import VersionNotice from '../components/VersionNotice.astro';
import { release, releaseURL, packetExample, source } from '../data/site';
---
<Base title="Livewire" description="Bring recorded network exchanges back to a live target. Fresh application sessions, ordered packet replay, and evidence you can inspect. Open source. Runs locally.">
  <section class="hero wrap">
    <div class="hero-copy"><a class="release-pill" href={releaseURL}><strong>v{release.version}</strong> Open source network replay <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a><h1>Put your packet<br />capture <em>back<br class="desktop-break" /> to work.</em></h1><p class="lede">Turn a recorded exchange into a repeatable test. Open fresh sessions against a live target, or send the original packets—and see exactly what happened.</p><div class="actions"><a class="button" href={sitePath("/install/")}>Get Livewire <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a><a class="button button-secondary" href={sitePath("/workflows/")}>Explore the workflows <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></div><div class="hero-foot"><span>Windows & Linux</span><span>No cloud required</span><span>MIT licensed</span></div></div>
    <Flow />
  </section>
  <div class="wrap"><div class="protocol-strip"><span class="eyebrow">FROM FIELD SYSTEMS<br />TO WEB SERVICES</span><div class="protocol-names"><span>Modbus</span><span>DNP3</span><span>HTTP/1</span><span>MQTT</span><span>DNS</span><span>TLS</span></div><a href={sitePath("/protocols/")}>Full protocol guide ↗</a></div></div>
  <section class="section wrap" id="workflows"><div class="section-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">ONE CAPTURE. TWO INTENTS.</span><h2>Test the conversation.<br />Or replay the packets.</h2></div><p>Choose the evidence you need. Application behavior and packet transmission answer different questions.</p></div><div class="workflow-grid"><article class="workflow"><div class="workflow-label"><span>01 / STATEFUL</span><span>FRESH CONNECTIONS</span></div><h3>Bring the exchange to life.</h3><p><code>live</code> sends recovered requests through new TCP/TLS sessions. Supported adapters follow live protocol state and compare checked responses. TLS without matching secrets performs a fresh handshake only.</p><Code code={"livewire live issue.pcap -t 192.0.2.50"} label={`Fresh application replay · v${release.version}`} /><a class="text-link" href={sitePath("/workflows/#live")}>Run a live session <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></article><article class="workflow"><div class="workflow-label"><span>02 / STATELESS</span><span>RECORDED FRAMES</span></div><h3>Put the recording on the wire.</h3><p>Send captured frame bytes in capture order, with the pacing you select. Packet replay does not establish a new session or verify target responses.</p><Code code={packetExample} label={`Stateless packet replay · v${release.version}`} /><a class="text-link" href={sitePath("/workflows/#packets")}>Replay recorded packets <span aria-hidden="true">→</span></a></article></div><VersionNotice /></section>
  <section class="section wrap" id="tls-recording"><div class="section-heading"><div><span class="eyebrow">TLS APPLICATION REPLAY</span><h2>Record the secure exchange.<br />Keep one replayable file.</h2></div><p>Capture a supported application's traffic and exported TLS secrets together. Replay its requests over fresh verified TLS connections, including Modbus, MQTT and DNP3.</p></div><Code code={"livewire capture -i <interface> -o issue.pcapng -tls -- <application> [args...]\nlivewire live issue.pcapng -t device.example:1502"} label="One PCAPNG · fresh TLS application replay" /><p>The recording application must support TLS key export. No separate key-log file or HTTP request file is needed afterward. <a class="text-link" href={sitePath("/secure-replay/#record")}>Record a TLS application →</a></p></section>
  <section class="evidence-section"><div class="section wrap evidence-grid"><div><span class="eyebrow">EVIDENCE, NOT ASSUMPTIONS</span><h2>A successful send<br />is only the start.</h2><p>Field issues are hard enough to reproduce. Your replay tool should make the result clear: what was sent, what came back, and what could actually be checked.</p><a class="text-link" href={sitePath("/releases/#qualification")}>Read the qualification record <span aria-hidden="true">↗</span></a></div><div class="evidence-rows"><article class="evidence-row"><span>01</span><div><h3>Fresh transport. Live application state.</h3><p>Use new connections and supported protocol adapters. Captured TCP state and old TLS ciphertext are not reused as a live application session.</p></div></article><article class="evidence-row"><span>02</span><div><h3>Results with explicit limits.</h3><p>Separate checked response matches, differences, incomplete exchanges, and unverified transmission. Matching responses alone do not prove a device fault recurred.</p></div></article><article class="evidence-row"><span>03</span><div><h3>Your lab stays local.</h3><p>Captures, matching TLS key logs, credentials, and replay traffic stay on your machine and your chosen target. This website only serves documentation.</p></div></article></div></div></section>
  <section class="get-started wrap"><div><span class="eyebrow">START WITH WHAT YOU RECORDED</span><h2>Inspect first. Replay with intent.</h2></div><div class="actions"><a class="button" href={sitePath("/install/")}>Install Livewire <span aria-hidden="true">↓</span></a><a class="text-link" href={source('docs/RELIABILITY_IMPLEMENTATION.md')}>Read the technical guide ↗</a></div></section>
</Base>
